<title>USA: Midland sets an extra $5.50 dividend.</title>
<headline>Midland sets an extra $5.50 dividend.</headline>
<dateline>WAYNE, N.J. 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Midland Bancorp Inc said on Friday it set an extra dividend of $5.50 in addition to its previously declared $2.00 dividend.</p>
<p>The extra dividend is payable to its shareholders on October 1, the company said.   Midland said its dividends will</p>
<p>be increased overall because of the just-announced merger of Midland into Valley National Bancorp.</p>
<p>The increased dividends will reflect the new equivalent exchange ratio, the company said.  Valley and Midland said Valley would offer 30 shares of its stock for every Midland share as part of the merger deal.</p>
</text>
